    {
      "uid": "m1jWigDJI",
      "markdown": "- **Why it matters:** with `secure_password_change = false`, any session of the space account can call `PUT /auth/v1/user` and set a new password. A handed-over session could do that, then sign in with the new password and get sessions that are not in the registry, so per-session sign-out no longer cuts it off. The change also signs out every other session of the account (`LogoutAllExceptMe` in `internal/models/user.go`), and the plugins cannot sign back in with the old password. `agent-read-only-access` records the same endpoint behaviour in its design. <roam uid=\"m1jWigDJI\"/>\n",
      "path": [
        "Spec: MCP token handoff <roam uid=\"kPg_0_-lh\" refs=\"9\"/>",
        "Design <roam uid=\"-0hMsmA6D\" heading=\"2\"/>",
        "Decisions <roam uid=\"fGkowLhCM\" heading=\"3\"/>",
        "**Can the MCP change the space password?** <roam uid=\"diG1qynhh\"/>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "uid": "3c62wvZ1I",
      "markdown": "- **Why:** (a) cannot be revoked short of rotating the signing key, and `agent-read-only-access` records that the project uses asymmetric keys whose private half cannot be extracted. (b) cannot be revoked without changing the password for every plugin instance. (c) needs a person to type the space password into a consent page, and today the password never leaves the plugin. (d) uses refresh and sign-out as they already work. <roam uid=\"3c62wvZ1I\"/>\n",
